A $2$ m post casts a shadow $3$ m long.
At the same time a building casts a shadow $18$ m long.
Find the height of the building.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,1.6);
\draw (0,0) -- (2.4,0) node[midway,below] {$18\text{ m}$};
\draw (2.4,0) -- (0,1.6);
\node[left] at (0,0.8) {$h$};
\draw (3.4,0) -- (3.4,0.267);
\draw (3.4,0) -- (3.8,0) node[midway,below] {$3\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.8,0) -- (3.4,0.267);
\node[left] at (3.4,0.134) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A $10$ m tree casts a shadow $4$ m long.
At the same time a shrub beside it casts a shadow $1$ m long.
Find the height of the shrub.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,2.4);
\draw (0,0) -- (0.96,0) node[midway,below] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw (0.96,0) -- (0,2.4);
\node[left] at (0,1.2) {$10\text{ m}$};
\draw (1.96,0) -- (1.96,0.6);
\draw (1.96,0) -- (2.2,0) node[midway,below] {$1\text{ m}$};
\draw (2.2,0) -- (1.96,0.6);
\node[left] at (1.96,0.3) {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A $1.5$ m post casts a shadow $2$ m long.
At the same time a $9$ m tower stands nearby.
Find the length of the tower's shadow.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,1.8);
\draw (0,0) -- (2.4,0) node[midway,below] {$s$};
\draw (2.4,0) -- (0,1.8);
\node[left] at (0,0.9) {$9\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.4,0) -- (3.4,0.3);
\draw (3.4,0) -- (3.8,0) node[midway,below] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.8,0) -- (3.4,0.3);
\node[left] at (3.4,0.15) {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A street lamp is $8$ m high.
A person stands $9$ m from its base and casts a shadow $3$ m long.
Find the height of the person.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (1.05,0) node[midway,below] {$3\text{ m}$};
\draw (1.05,0) -- (4.2,0) node[midway,below] {$9\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,0) -- (4.2,2.8);
\draw (1.05,0) -- (1.05,0.7);
\draw (4.2,0) -- (4.2,2.8) node[midway,right] {$8\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (1.05,0.35) {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two cables support a vertical pole at the same angle.
The cables are $5$ m and $15$ m long, and the shorter cable reaches $4$ m up the pole.
Find the height of the pole.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (-1.44,0) -- (0,0);
\draw (0,0) -- (0,1.92);
\draw[gray] (0.22,0) -- (0.22,0.64) node[midway,right] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw (-1.44,0) -- (0,1.92) node[midway,above left] {$15\text{ m}$};
\draw (-0.48,0) -- (0,0.64) node[midway,above left] {$5\text{ m}$};
\draw (-0.15,0) -- (-0.15,0.15) -- (0,0.15);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A surveyor sets up two similar triangles to find the width $w$ across a gully, as shown.
Find $w$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (-0.4,0) -- (0,0);
\draw (0,0) -- (0.96,0) node[midway,above] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw (0.96,0) -- (3.84,0) node[midway,above] {$w$};
\draw (3.84,0) -- (4.2,0);
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.72) node[midway,left] {$3\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.84,0) -- (3.84,2.16) node[midway,right] {$9\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (0,-0.72) -- (3.84,2.16);
\draw (3.24,2.16) -- (4.44,2.16);
\node[above right] at (3.84,2.16) {Post};
\draw (0,-0.15) -- (0.15,-0.15) -- (0.15,0);
\draw (3.69,0) -- (3.69,0.15) -- (3.84,0.15);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A person $1.5$ m tall stands $5$ m from a lamp post and casts a shadow $2.5$ m long.
Find the height of the lamp post.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (1.125,0) node[midway,below] {$2.5\text{ m}$};
\draw (1.125,0) -- (3.375,0) node[midway,below] {$5\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,0) -- (3.375,2.025);
\draw (1.125,0) -- (1.125,0.675) node[midway,left] {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.375,0) -- (3.375,2.025) node[midway,right] {$H$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A child $1.2$ m tall and a $6$ m lamppost cast shadows at the same time of day.
The lamppost's shadow is $8$ m longer than the child's shadow.
Find the length of the child's shadow.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,0.288);
\draw (0,0) -- (0.48,0) node[midway,below] {$d$};
\draw (0.48,0) -- (0,0.288);
\node[left] at (0,0.144) {$1.2\text{ m}$};
\draw (2.2,0) -- (2.2,1.44);
\draw (2.2,0) -- (4.6,0) node[midway,below] {$d+8$};
\draw (4.6,0) -- (2.2,1.44);
\node[left] at (2.2,0.72) {$6\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
